# Slabhold workflow (Windows PowerShell)
- Terminal is Windows PowerShell. Chain commands with ; not &&. Use npx.cmd, not npx.
- Supabase CLI is installed and linked to project knuwflptobyutrauxblj.
- After finishing any task, do these steps yourself in the terminal, in order, and show me the output of each:
  1. Run npm test and npm run build. Stop and fix if either fails.
  2. If you created a new file in supabase/migrations, run: npx.cmd supabase db push   (answer Y if asked). Never edit an old migration; always make a new one. Never run destructive SQL (drop table, delete from user tables, truncate) without asking me first.
  3. Run: git add -A; git commit -m "<short summary>"; git push
  4. If pricing/comps/card_values logic changed, wait ~90 seconds for Vercel, then run:
     $s = (Select-String CRON_SECRET .env.local).Line.Split('=',2)[1].Trim(); Invoke-RestMethod https://slabhold.vercel.app/api/cron/refresh-card-values -Headers @{Authorization="Bearer $s"}
- Never print, commit or paste secrets from .env.local.
- Never run test scripts that insert or delete data as real users on production.
- At the end, give me a 2-line summary: what changed, and "Ready for QA".
